Other interactions:
* {{dlc|nr}} {{i|Dead Eye}}: Only Isaac's tears affect the damage multiplier.
* {{i|Dr. Fetus}}: A dangerous combination, since familiars naturally stay behind the character, and the character's movement may block the bomb, which causes self-damage easily.
* {{dlc+|a+nr}} {{C|The Forgotten}}: Fires bone tears like {{i|Compound Fracture}} without the splitting effect. Reverts to normal tears when switching to {{c|The Soul}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{i|Flat Stone|a+nr}}: The effective range of Incubus' tears is roughly doubled, with a single bounce in the middle of the flight.
* {{i|Guillotine}}: Incubus will fire tears in relative position to its body depending on where Isaac's head is currently.
* {{Dlc|nr}} {{i|Isaac's Tears}}: The item is recharged by Isaac's tears, not Incubus'. This item works with {{C|Lilith}}.
** {{Dlc|r}} Incubus' tears contribute to the item charge.
* {{i|Kidney Stone}}: Incubus ignores the range down from this item, and will fire the tear barrage but not the stone.
** {{Dlc|r}} Incubus is still able to fire tears while Kidney Stone is charging.
* {{i|The Ludovico Technique|nr}}: Incubus' tears become piercing and spectral but otherwise fires normal tears.
* {{i|My Reflection|nr}}: Since Incubus ignores shot speed the tears turn back very quickly, greatly reducing effective range.
* {{i|Tech X|anr}}: Incubus shoots small, fixed-size Tech X laser rings, with a very slightly longer minimum charge than Isaac.

